<title>USA: RESEARCH ALERT - Boeing buy reiterated.</title>
<headline>RESEARCH ALERT - Boeing buy reiterated.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gruntal &amp; Co said it reiterated a buy rating on Boeing Co.</p>
<p>-- said raised 1998 earnings estimates to $3.50 a share from $3.40 a share.</p>
<p>-- said investors should buy on weakness or if the shares broke through $58.</p>
<p>-- The Federal Trade Commission approved the proposed merger with McDonnell Douglas Corp on the condition Boeing not accept any more &quot;exclusive&quot; supplier contracts with airlines.  Said that condition is actually good news for Boeing.  Said all Boeing got out of those deals was &quot;production predictability,&quot; which the company does not need anyway.  Said airlines will probably buy Boeing planes anyway as they rationalize their fleet and control costs.</p>
<p>-- Boeing gained 1-2/16 to 55-15/16.</p>
</text>
